{"id":"chatcmpl-a385ab56-1937-434b-bf22-cc58c1fde47e","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250383,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first diagnostic workflow: first query a domain expert tool to narrow the hypothesis space (presence, laterality, size), then independently confirm the leading hypothesis using a grounded localization tool before committing to an answer. The pattern emphasizes cross-checking a candidate finding with a second, spatially-grounded method and using image markers (e.g., laterality labels) to validate orientation. This reduces laterality/side-confusion errors common in medical image interpretation.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Use a domain-expert query tool first to extract discriminating attributes (presence, side, size) that separate the answer options.\",\n    \"Independently verify the leading candidate with a grounded localization tool that returns spatial evidence, rather than relying on a single source.\",\n    \"Check image orientation markers (e.g., laterality labels) to confirm left/right before finalizing any side-dependent answer.\",\n    \"Structure reasoning to explicitly map tool evidence to each option, eliminating alternatives before selecting the answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Query an expert model for the key discriminating finding, then confirm with a localization/grounding tool; always validate laterality against image markers.\",\n    \"Multiple-choice diagnostic tasks\": \"Identify the attribute that distinguishes options (side, size, location), gather evidence for that attribute specifically, and eliminate options one by one.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted verification\": \"Pair a broad analytical tool with a narrow grounding tool so conclusions are corroborated by two independent evidence types before answering.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the discriminating attribute (e.g., left vs right, small vs large) is explicitly supported by tool evidence.\",\n    \"Verify image orientation/laterality markers match the reported finding before submitting the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":450,"total_tokens":825,"completion_tokens":375,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":450},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":375}}}